{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And she emptied.</b> A term of pouring out. And there are many in the language of Mishnah: הַמְעָרֶה מִכְּלִי אֶל כְּלִי — pouring from vessel to vessel. And in Scripture it has a parallel: ״אַל תְּעַר נַפְשִׁי״ (Psalms 141), ״אֲשֶׁר הֶעֱרָה לַמָּוֶת נַפְשׁוֹ״ (Isaiah 53)." "<b>Let them drink.</b> A hollowed-out stone into which the camels drink."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:09.875042159Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}